            <div xml:id="d186">

                <pb facs="0265" n="231" sameAs="frus:frus1870/pg231"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">No. 186.</note>
                <head>Mr. Fish to Baron
                        Gerolt.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1870-10-22"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >October</hi> 22, 1870.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>The undersigned, Secretary of State of the United States, has the honor to
                    acknowledge the receipt of the note of the 17th instant addressed to him by the
                    Baron Gerolt, the envoy extraordinary and minister plenipotentiary of the North
                    German Union, inclosing a copy of a dispatch from the chancellor of his
                    government of the 27th ultimo, giving a statement of the negotiations which took
                    place between himself and Mr. Jules Favre.</p>
                <p>The undersigned begs the Baron Gerolt to accept a renewed assurance of his
                    highest consideration.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>HAMILTON FISH.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
